    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 tests passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nIntroduced address normalization on the `POST /api/owners` create pipeline so the stored and returned `address` is always the normalized form.\n\n**New file \u2014 `AddressNormalizer.java`**: a small final helper (mirroring the existing `E164Telephone`) with a static, idempotent `normalize(String)` that trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands whole-word abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). Null/whitespace-only input normalizes to `\"\"`.\n\n**`ValidateOwnerFields.java`** (first pipeline step): normalizes the address in place *before* the required-field check, so the address is stored/returned normalized and a blank-after-normalization address (e.g. `\"   \"`) is rejected as a 400 naming `address`.\n\n**`EnsureUniqueHousehold.java`** and **`AssignHousehold.java`**: address comparisons \u2014 for both duplicate detection and the derived shared `householdId` \u2014 now use `AddressNormalizer.normalize` on both the request and each existing owner, so `12 main st` and `12  Main  Street` are treated as the same household. Last-name comparison is unchanged.\n\nBecause normalization runs in the first step, every downstream step (build/mapper, household checks, save, response) sees the already-normalized value, keeping storage, return, and all address comparisons on one canonical form.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (whitespace/case, abbreviation expansion, blank-after-normalize rejection) \u2014 3/3 pass; full `mvnw test` is green.",
